WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Blueprint is an AI testbed for real-world drawings.
Give an agent a task. Inspect its actions. Measure the result.

00:08.000 --> 00:18.000
One drawing. One question: what is the floor area of the fitness room?
Measure to the inner walls.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.000
A saved DeepSeek run uses OCR to locate the room label.

00:22.000 --> 00:25.000
Geometry tools inspect the room's wall lines.

00:25.000 --> 00:29.000
The drawing scale converts pixels into a measured area.
The tool calls and submitted evidence can be replayed.

00:29.000 --> 00:34.000
A boundary decision changes the estimate.
The saved run treats this line as furniture or equipment.

00:34.000 --> 00:39.000
It submits 29.1 square metres.
Its selected region extends above the reference inner-wall boundary.

00:39.000 --> 00:44.000
Same drawing, same task: DeepSeek submits 29.1 square metres.
Kimi submits 26.4 square metres.

00:44.000 --> 00:49.000
The reference is 26.9 square metres, with a 2% numeric tolerance.
A plausible explanation is not enough. The result must survive a check.

00:49.000 --> 00:56.000
Repeatable tasks give feedback on quantity, evidence and confidence.
36 construction tasks. 72 saved AI runs.

00:56.000 --> 01:00.000
A separate research extension: what if the evidence is a field of light?
hBN is a layered crystal.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
Infrared light couples to crystal vibrations.
The cavity's shape controls how the coupled waves fit inside it.

01:04.000 --> 01:14.000
The hBN nanocavity explorer makes the physics visible.
Explore interactive field and mode views from precomputed research data.

01:14.000 --> 01:19.000
Your turn. Follow the task and check the evidence.
Open the web demo. No account or password required.

01:19.000 --> 01:24.000
Blueprint. Make the answer inspectable.
Explore the public web demo.
